The issue is that we are mixing **Spring Data JPA (voucherPostingRepository.save(posting))** with **Database Defaults**.
When you instantiate a new VoucherPosting object in Java, any boolean or string field you don't explicitly set becomes null in Java. If your database table has a default constraint (or if a previous developer hardcoded a trigger) that says "If IS_SCHEDULE_OVERRIDE is null, make it 'YES'", then it will silently flip it in Oracle.
Furthermore, we missed a mapping in createBatchRequest (the manual entry method), and the redundancy in VOUCHER_POSTING_DATA is happening because we didn't remove the columns from the DB table.
Let's fix this definitively.
