### 4. Ensure VoucherPosting.java Entity is Correct
For Hibernate to save these fields to VOUCHER_POSTING, the Java entity must have the exact correct naming convention.
Double check your VoucherPosting.java entity class. Make sure these three fields exist and are mapped exactly like this:
```java
    @Column(name = "WORKFLOW_CODE", length = 100)
    private String workflowCode;

    @Column(name = "COMMON_BATCH_REMARKS", length = 30)
    private String commonBatchRemarks;

    @Column(name = "CREATOR_ROLE")
    private Integer creatorRole;

```
If your entity has different names (e.g., batchRemarks instead of commonBatchRemarks), the posting.setCommonBatchRemarks(dto.getCommonBatchRemarks()) call will save it to the wrong property, resulting in null in the database.
